"rules_info_app" = "<b><AppName/></b> is a <b>fan app</b> created with passion for all retrogaming lovers. It allows you to play the great classics of consoles such as <b>Game Boy</b>, <b>Game Boy Color</b>, <b>Game Boy Advance</b>, <b>NES</b>, <b>SNES</b> and <b>Nintendo 64</b>, directly from your device, with the ability to <b>save progress on servers</b> and resume the game from where you left off, even on other devices.\n\nWe would like to clarify that <b><AppName/></b> is <b>not affiliated in any way with <m>Nintendo Co., Ltd.</m></b>. All names, registered trademarks and logos are the property of their respective owners and are mentioned for <m>descriptive purposes</m> only.\n\n<b>Credits</b>\nA special thanks to those who contributed with talent and passion:\n\n• <b>Grant Gliner</b> (<m>@glinstagrant</m>) – <m>Pause Menu Icons</m>\n• <b>Eric Lewis</b> (<m>github.com/ericlewis</m>) – <m>Dark Mode</m>\n• <b>Chris Rittenhouse</b> (<m>litritt.com</m>) – <m>Genesis Skin</m>, <m>Show Status Bar</m>, <m>Game Screenshots</m>, <m>Toast Notifications</m>, <m>Alternate App Icons</m>\n• <b>Noah Keck</b> (<m>github.com/noah978</m>) – <m>CheatBase</m>\n• <b>Ian Clawson</b> (<m>github.com/ianclawson</m>) – <m>Local Multiplayer</m>\n• <b>Domenico Gonnelli</b> – <m>Developer Apple 2025</m>\n• <b>Freepik</b> – for some graphic resources used\n\n<b>Licenses</b>\nThe app uses open source software components and licensed libraries, including:\n\n• <b>SQLite.swift</b> by <m>Stephen Celis</m>\n• <b>SDWebImage</b> by <m>Olivier Poitrey</m>\n• <b>ZIPFoundation</b> by <m>Thomas Zoechling</m>\n• <b>SwiftyDropbox</b> by <m>Dropbox Inc.</m>\n• <b>Google API Objective-C Client</b> – <m>Apache License 2.0</m>\n• <b>SMCalloutView</b> by <m>Nick Farina</m> – <m>Apache License 2.0</m>\n\n<b>Emulators</b>\nThis app integrates the following emulation cores:\n\n<m>GNU GPL v3</m> license:\n• Nestopia\n• mupen64plus\n• Gambatte\n• visualboyadvance-m\n• DeSmuME\n• melonDS\n\nSpecific licenses:\n• Snes9x\n• Genesis Plus GX\n\n<b>Artwork</b>\nGame images are managed automatically thanks to the support of <m>OpenVGDB</m>.\n\nThank you for using <b><AppName/></b> and have fun with your favorite titles!";


